    {
      "body": "Good news: the `tmp/surya_workshop` part is just where the repo happens to live on disk here \u2014 Git only tracks paths **relative to the repo root** (which is `/home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop`), so on GitHub your files show up as `downstream_apps/flare_forecast/...` regardless. Nothing to configure for that \u2014 it already works. You're on branch `downstream/flare_forecast`, tracking `origin/downstream/flare_forecast`, and up to date (no conflicts).\n\nBefore I commit everything, two things worth flagging:\n\n1. **`.chat` files** (`checks-help.chat`, `image_flip.chat`, `plots-xclass-check.chat`, `untitled.chat`) \u2014 these are Jupyter AI chat session logs, not code. Do you want these pushed to GitHub, or should I leave them untracked/gitignored?\n2. **`s3_cache_dir`** changed in both `downstream_apps/flare_forecast/configs/config_script.yaml` and `downstream_apps/template/configs/config_script.yaml` to `/home/jovyan/scratch_space/surya_cache` \u2014 that's a machine-specific path. If it's just local scratch space for this JupyterLab instance, you may not want to push that (it'd break for anyone else, and the template one especially looks like it wasn't meant to change). Include both, one, or neither?\n\nLet me know how you want those two handled, and I'll stage, commit, and push the rest (the notebooks, `datasets/flare_dataset.py`, and the intentional config change to `time_delta_input_minutes`/`time_dim`).",
